WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:05.470
Some of the most famous and notable SCPs in
the database are what some of us would call

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:06.470
monsters.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:09.670
I bet you can think of some off the top of
your head, right?

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:14.330
Everyone even loosely familiar with the SCP
Foundation can recall some anomalies that

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:19.490
are famous not because of their history, or
their power, but because of their terrifying

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.400
tendency to prey on humans indiscriminately.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:28.500
There’s the legendary SCP-682, which is
the perfect predator.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.309
Invulnerable to any kind of attack or wound,
it instantly adapts to whatever was used to

00:00:33.309 --> 00:00:36.989
attack it and regenerates any lost flesh or
material.

00:00:36.989 --> 00:00:43.089
It’s not just hard to kill - it can be downright
impossible, though the Foundation is constantly

00:00:43.089 --> 00:00:47.149
working on some new technique and hoping for
success.

00:00:47.149 --> 00:00:52.399
In case that wasn’t all terrible enough,
it’s also actively hateful of all life around

00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:55.499
it, seeking to exterminate every living thing.

00:00:55.499 --> 00:01:02.270
Or take SCP-939, a pack of four-legged beasts
with bright red skin and ice-cold bodies.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:07.380
They work together to lure in prey and tear
unsuspecting researchers and civilians to

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.940
pieces with their long, sharp teeth.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:14.560
You might be thinking that their tactics don’t
sound too different from any other pack predator,

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:16.880
like wolves or coyotes.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:21.930
But wolves and coyotes don’t steal the voices
of people they’ve eaten, then use the voices

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:24.180
to lure in other humans.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:29.900
Needless to say, the SCP-939 instances are
under intense surveillance.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:33.040
And who can forget about SCP-106?

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:38.700
The famous Old Man, who preys upon the living
and sucks the unwary children and D-class

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:44.390
into his pocket dimension, where he can engage
in an eternal game of cat-and-mouse with them.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:50.280
Unlike the others, SCP-106 isn’t just predatory,
it’s downright sadistic.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:56.280
It likes to play with its food and enjoys
the struggle of watching them try to escape.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:00.600
The Foundation barely has a handle on how
to contain it, and they’re constantly hoping

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:05.740
that it doesn’t try to breach containment
and result in even more innocent casualties.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:10.849
You can see why the SCP Foundation is so wary
and paranoid about SCPs that are predators

00:02:10.849 --> 00:02:12.130
preying on humans.

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:18.930
At least not directly.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:24.779
Instead, SCP-1788 is a specific kind of process,
treatment, or ritual.

00:02:24.779 --> 00:02:29.130
The Foundation’s researchers aren’t totally
confident on what it is yet, but they know

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:35.230
that whatever it is, it causes a frightening,
horrifying transformation on whoever the unwilling

00:02:36.885 --> 00:02:41.775
We call these creatures SCP-1788-1 instances.

00:02:41.775 --> 00:02:48.236
The Foundation currently has no idea who or
what created SCP-1788 and why, but they’re

00:02:48.236 --> 00:02:53.266
performing active and constant research, including
investigating all the groups of interest who

00:02:59.273 --> 00:03:03.982
They’re almost always obese - in fact, once
they’re fully grown, they appear anywhere

00:03:03.982 --> 00:03:06.982
from a hundred and fifty to two hundred kilograms.

00:03:06.982 --> 00:03:12.213
But don’t be fooled by appearances - they
might look like they’re simply fat, but

00:03:12.213 --> 00:03:17.033
the insides of their bodies are filled with
muscle and dense bone, making them easily

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:21.132
two-hundred and fifty to three hundred kilograms
in actual weight.

00:03:21.132 --> 00:03:25.762
We’ll go into their internal anatomy more
in a second, but for now let's return to the

00:03:25.762 --> 00:03:27.923
outside of their bodies.

00:03:27.923 --> 00:03:31.833
When you look at someone’s face, what’s
the first thing you notice?

00:03:31.833 --> 00:03:37.563
It can be their nose, their hair, but nine
times out of ten, it’s probably their eyes.

00:03:37.563 --> 00:03:43.663
And SCP-1788-1 instances might fool you in
that regard - their eyes are slightly too

00:03:43.663 --> 00:03:48.613
large for their face, just enough to weird
you out if you looked at them, though you

00:03:48.613 --> 00:03:53.452
probably wouldn’t be able to put your finger
on what exactly was wrong about them.

00:03:53.452 --> 00:03:58.822
When instances get hot and perspire, their
sweat is chemically unbalanced - it has high

00:03:58.822 --> 00:04:03.822
levels of potassium and copper, enough to
show up on tests but still firmly in the normal

00:04:03.822 --> 00:04:05.993
range for adult humans.

00:04:05.993 --> 00:04:11.873
As you can see, the changes to SCP-1788-1
instances from the outside are pretty hard

00:04:11.873 --> 00:04:12.873
to tell.

00:04:12.873 --> 00:04:16.232
But on the inside, it’s a totally different
story.

00:04:16.232 --> 00:04:20.063
Their internal anatomy has been extensively
changed.

00:04:20.063 --> 00:04:24.193
During the first dissections, the Foundation
researchers didn’t even realize these creatures

00:04:24.193 --> 00:04:26.442
were originally human at first.

00:04:26.442 --> 00:04:32.164
The instances’ long bones, such as the ones
in their arms and legs, and cranium, are super

00:04:32.164 --> 00:04:36.063
dense and thick, more so than any normal human.

00:04:36.063 --> 00:04:40.313
And they’re not just made of bone, either
- they’re interwoven with thick strands

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:44.653
of heavy metals, making them super-strong
and powerful.

00:04:44.653 --> 00:04:48.903
Their muscles, on the other hand, have been
reinforced in a totally different way.

00:04:48.903 --> 00:04:53.093
The researchers are still studying tissue
samples, but it seems that the muscle fibers

00:04:53.093 --> 00:04:57.933
have been modified into shapes resembling
carbon nanotubes, molecular structures that

00:04:57.933 --> 00:05:01.882
are super-light while still being stronger
than steel.

00:05:01.882 --> 00:05:06.463
Evidence derived from numerous physical tests
run on the instances have shown that because

00:05:06.463 --> 00:05:14.452
of these structural modifications, SCP-1788-1
instances are much, much stronger, faster,

00:05:14.452 --> 00:05:20.823
and have the ability to withstand punishment
far beyond the threshold of any normal humans.

00:05:20.823 --> 00:05:26.923
SCP-1788-1 instances also possess redundant
organ systems for several of the human body’s

00:05:26.923 --> 00:05:30.512
vital processes - backup organs, basically.

00:05:30.512 --> 00:05:37.403
When one of a normal human's primary organs
stop working, they usually die, but SCP-1788-1

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:41.452
instances can just switch to using the backup
organ and keep going.

00:05:41.452 --> 00:05:46.243
The most obvious example is the fact that
they have a second heart, and it can either

00:05:46.243 --> 00:05:50.553
function independently if the main heart stops
working, or it can work together with the

00:05:50.553 --> 00:05:55.042
main heart to give the instance much faster
respiration and breathing abilities.

00:05:55.042 --> 00:05:58.192
That’s part of why they’re able to move
so fast.

00:05:58.192 --> 00:06:02.232
Speaking of their circulatory system, some
of their blood vessels have locks that can

00:06:08.789 --> 00:06:10.109
organs.

00:06:10.109 --> 00:06:15.059
That’s right; SCP-1788-1 instances have
a second brain.

00:06:15.059 --> 00:06:21.538
Rather than in the head, the second brain
is located in the chest inside its own ribcage.

00:06:21.538 --> 00:06:27.409
The researchers are baffled by this part of
the SCP-1788-1 instance’s anatomy - they

00:06:27.409 --> 00:06:31.219
haven’t been able to figure out what this
brain does normally when the first brain is

00:06:31.219 --> 00:06:32.219
still working.

00:06:32.219 --> 00:06:37.079
But they have seen that if the first brain
is destroyed, this second brain can take over

00:06:37.079 --> 00:06:38.439
to some limited capacity.

00:06:38.439 --> 00:06:45.689
They saw this firsthand when a team of Foundation
agents lured an SCP-1788-1 instance into a

00:06:45.689 --> 00:06:49.069
killzone, and an MTF sniper blew open its
head.

00:06:49.069 --> 00:06:54.050
But despite its brain and most of its sensory
function being utterly destroyed, the monster

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:58.979
kept going and was able to subdue other agents
before being brought down.

00:06:58.979 --> 00:07:04.959
Another main difference in the overall anatomy
of an SCP-1788-1 instance from a normal human

00:07:04.959 --> 00:07:06.299
is its arms.

00:07:06.299 --> 00:07:09.859
More specifically, that it has extra arms.

00:07:09.859 --> 00:07:15.079
A second pair of arms sit just below the regular
main arms, extending out of the armpits.

00:07:15.079 --> 00:07:19.999
They’re much smaller, but they’re just
as strong and flexible, and testing has shown

00:07:19.999 --> 00:07:26.299
that SCP-1788-1 instances can use all four
arms at the same time if they need to.

00:07:26.299 --> 00:07:30.519
But to maintain their cover, most of the time
instances just hold the second arms folded

00:07:30.519 --> 00:07:35.379
up and close to their sides, where nobody
can tell they’re there from the instances’

00:07:35.379 --> 00:07:36.759
massive size.

00:07:36.759 --> 00:07:40.819
When an instance is wearing clothes and has
their arms folded up, it’s almost impossible

00:07:40.819 --> 00:07:48.609
to tell which is an SCP-1788-1 instance and
which is just a normal, if obese human being.

00:07:48.609 --> 00:07:54.559
As you can see, SCP-1788 causes quite a few
drastic changes to the human body.

00:07:54.559 --> 00:07:59.839
In fact, you could probably say that these
creatures aren’t even properly human anymore.

00:07:59.839 --> 00:08:06.839
But despite all these changes, SCP-1788-1
instances are, as you can also see, really

00:08:06.839 --> 00:08:09.959
hard to differentiate from regular humans.

00:08:09.959 --> 00:08:11.579
The perfect stealth predator, right?

00:08:11.579 --> 00:08:17.249
But what exactly do instances do with all
these additional abilities and modifications?

00:08:17.249 --> 00:08:24.838
Well, like we said, the second part of SCP-1788
changes the behavior of the people it infects.

00:08:24.838 --> 00:08:26.989
Namely, they become...

00:08:26.989 --> 00:08:28.158
predatory.

00:08:28.158 --> 00:08:33.658
The behavior of SCP-1788 instances was hard
to observe, since finding them at all was

00:08:33.658 --> 00:08:40.408
such a difficult task, but eventually the
research team located a large group of SCP-1788-1

00:08:40.408 --> 00:08:43.309
instances living in the same large metropolitan
city.

00:08:43.309 --> 00:08:49.028
The Foundation set up covert observation teams,
stakeouts, reconnaissance agents, and essentially

00:08:49.028 --> 00:08:52.209
blanketed the city in a net of surveillance.

00:08:52.209 --> 00:08:58.169
Before long, every little movement and action
of the SCP-1788-1 instances was recorded in

00:08:58.169 --> 00:08:59.739
the Foundation's database.

00:08:59.739 --> 00:09:05.889
They observed that as soon as SCP-1788-1 instances
hit adulthood, they would typically settle

00:09:05.889 --> 00:09:10.299
down in large cities, just like the one the
Foundation was staking out.

00:09:10.299 --> 00:09:15.049
They'd find a job - most would be in white
collar work and middle-management, but one

00:09:15.049 --> 00:09:19.619
thing that became evident was that none of
them would ever work as teachers, nurses,

00:09:19.619 --> 00:09:23.249
or any other job where they would come into
regular contact with kids.

00:09:26.231 --> 00:09:30.252
Once the Foundation realized what was going
on, they also realized there was nothing else

00:09:30.252 --> 00:09:32.421
to learn from just observing them.

00:09:32.421 --> 00:09:37.052
They had to get an instance into containment
to try and interrogate them.

00:09:37.052 --> 00:09:41.932
A lot of good agents lost their lives in the
multiple attempts that were made to tranquilize,

00:09:41.932 --> 00:09:48.392
sedate, capture or otherwise lure SCP-1788-1
instances into containment, but eventually

00:09:48.392 --> 00:09:52.902
a few were shot up with enough tranquilizer
to bring down an elephant and dragged back

00:09:52.902 --> 00:09:54.041
to the site.

00:09:54.041 --> 00:09:59.532
But all attempts to force the SCP-1788-1 in
the containment cells to surrender any knowledge

00:09:59.532 --> 00:10:00.532
failed.

00:10:00.532 --> 00:10:06.772
They seemed invulnerable to pain - torture,
coercion, interrogation, all methods failed

00:10:06.772 --> 00:10:10.432
to glean any important knowledge about their
motives from them.

00:10:10.432 --> 00:10:12.762
But all the instances the Foundation captured...

00:10:12.762 --> 00:10:18.392
well, the personnel who contained and researched
them could only describe them as deeply evil.

00:10:18.392 --> 00:10:20.882
They were cruel and narcissistic.

00:10:20.882 --> 00:10:25.361
They would only speak to communicate their
superiority over their captors, and mock personnel

00:10:26.947 --> 00:10:29.667
They weren't stupid, though - quite the opposite.

00:10:29.667 --> 00:10:34.197
The researchers recorded very high IQs and
problem-solving skills during intelligence

00:10:34.197 --> 00:10:38.676
tests, and they'd often psychoanalyze their
own researchers into revealing details about

00:10:38.676 --> 00:10:39.676
themselves.

00:10:39.676 --> 00:10:44.936
It didn't take long for the Site Directors
to ban all human contact with captured instances,

00:10:44.936 --> 00:10:47.587
lest they manipulate personnel into freeing
them.

00:10:47.587 --> 00:10:51.917
Meanwhile, in the city, surveillance teams
were still monitoring instances that couldn't

00:10:51.917 --> 00:10:54.517
be captured by the Foundation's strike teams.

00:10:54.517 --> 00:10:58.517
They watched them at their jobs, in their
cars and at their homes.

00:10:58.517 --> 00:11:04.166
They noticed that despite there being about
half a dozen SCP-1788-1 instances in that

00:11:04.166 --> 00:11:09.467
one city, they seemed to intentionally avoid
each other at all costs.

00:11:09.467 --> 00:11:14.686
They took jobs at different companies, lived
in different parts of town, shopped at different

00:11:15.138 --> 00:11:22.247
By sheer coincidence, three SCP-1788-1 instances
showed up at the same sporting event.

00:11:22.247 --> 00:11:26.538
They seemed to instantly realize what was
going on, and all left the stands at the same

00:11:26.538 --> 00:11:27.538
time.

00:11:27.538 --> 00:11:30.898
The undercover agents on duty followed, and
tracked them to the bathrooms.

00:11:30.898 --> 00:11:34.247
There, they discovered a grisly sight.

00:11:34.247 --> 00:11:40.518
The SCP-1788-1 instances were in the deserted
bathroom, violently beating each other against

00:11:40.518 --> 00:11:43.078
the walls with all four of their fists.

00:11:43.078 --> 00:11:47.718
They were hitting hard, with no regard for
their 'cover' identities, and spraying blood

00:11:47.718 --> 00:11:49.018
against the floor.

00:11:49.018 --> 00:11:52.877
They were fighting not for survival, but to
establish dominance.

00:11:52.877 --> 00:11:56.458
The gender didn't seem to matter - the female
instance was fighting just as brutally as

00:11:56.458 --> 00:11:59.908
the two male ones, and being beaten just as
harshly.

00:11:59.908 --> 00:12:04.107
After several minutes of this violent show
of force, two of the instances retreated out

00:12:04.107 --> 00:12:08.268
of the bathroom, submitting the territory
to the dominant victor of the fight.

00:12:08.268 --> 00:12:10.578
They quickly left the event entirely.

00:12:10.578 --> 00:12:14.868
The Foundation confirmed this with the few
instances they had contained - when two were

00:12:14.868 --> 00:12:17.758
put in the same cell, they'd fight for dominance.

00:12:17.758 --> 00:12:21.547
They quickly realized it was important to
ensure that instances were kept separate at

00:12:21.547 --> 00:12:26.458
all times, lest they kill each other and rob
the Foundation of a living test subject.

00:12:26.458 --> 00:12:30.997
There weren't many instances to begin with
- while multiple of the monsters were observed

00:12:30.997 --> 00:12:38.437
in the same city, they kept a strict ratio
of 1 SCP-1788-1 instance for every 100,000

00:12:38.437 --> 00:12:39.437
humans.

00:12:39.437 --> 00:12:43.367
The same behavior apex predators like bears
and sharks practice.

00:12:43.367 --> 00:12:47.497
This behavior of avoiding each other happens
for almost the entire calendar year.

00:12:47.497 --> 00:12:51.488
At first, the Foundation thought this avoiding
practice never stopped.

00:12:51.488 --> 00:12:55.938
But about a year into the surveillance program,
something seemed to change.

00:12:55.938 --> 00:13:01.807
Several of the tagged SCP-1788-1 instances
in the city actively began to gravitate towards

00:13:01.807 --> 00:13:03.578
each other's territories.

00:13:03.578 --> 00:13:08.357
The Foundation prepared for the inevitably
brutal fights, but something even stranger

00:13:08.357 --> 00:13:11.998
happened - they met each other and didn't
fight.

00:13:11.998 --> 00:13:14.867
In fact, they went to each other's homes.

00:13:14.867 --> 00:13:21.888
The recon teams reported that the SCP-1788-1
instances were in fact mating with one another.

00:13:21.888 --> 00:13:26.018
Apparently an annual mating season caused
this change in behavior.

00:13:31.308 --> 00:13:36.878
Needless to say, SCP-1788-1 instances are
horrifying apex predators.

00:13:36.878 --> 00:13:40.398
The Foundation's research and observation
teams have gleaned quite a bit about their

00:13:40.398 --> 00:13:46.068
anatomy and behavior, respectively, but many
of the personnel still hold the burning question:

00:13:46.068 --> 00:13:47.068
why?

00:13:47.068 --> 00:13:50.938
Why do SCP-1788-1 instances hunt?

00:13:50.938 --> 00:13:52.178
What's the motivation?

00:13:52.178 --> 00:13:56.617
Well, their uncooperativeness with interviews
makes finding out any details into their thought

00:13:56.617 --> 00:13:58.528
process virtually impossible.

00:13:58.528 --> 00:14:03.378
However, there was one occurrence where one
of the captured instances accidentally let

00:14:03.378 --> 00:14:04.688
something slip.

00:14:04.688 --> 00:14:08.908
One of the Site Directors was attempting to
interrogate an instance using an electroshock

00:14:08.908 --> 00:14:09.908
collar.

00:14:18.577 --> 00:14:22.457
it gave a simple, sneering response: "Grow
up.

00:14:22.457 --> 00:14:23.547
Or die."

00:14:23.547 --> 00:14:29.787
Now go check out “SCP-5094 - Miss J's Whiz
Kidz Schoolhouse” and “SCP-053 - Young

00:14:29.787 --> 00:14:32.817
Girl” for more kid-related anomalies from
SCP Explained!

